fs></svg>"]],"body":{"Block":[]}}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"The "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"change of base"}]}},{"Text":" adjoints commute with reindexing along it: the canonical comparison maps"}]},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f^prime) g^* -> h^* scripts(∑)_(f) wide h^* scripts(∏)_(f) ->\nscripts(∏)_(f^prime) g^*"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"are isomorphisms, the second whenever "},{"Math":{"src":"C"}},{"Text":" is locally cartesian closed. This is the "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"Beck–Chevalley condition"}]},{"Text":", part of what it means for a fibration to have (co)products ("},{"Cite":{"key":"jacobs-1999","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":", Definition 1.9.4). For the codomain fibration "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(f)"}},{"Text":" is postcomposition with "},{"Math":{"src":"f"}},{"Text":", and the condition for "},{"Math":{"src":"∑"}},{"Text":" is the pasting lemma for pullbacks ("},{"Cite":{"key":"jacobs-1999","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":", Proposition 1.9.8). When every "},{"Math":{"src":"u^*"}},{"Text":" has both adjoints, the condition holds for "},{"Math":{"src":"∑"}},{"Text":" if and only if it holds for "},{"Math":{"src":"∏"}},{"Text":" ("},{"Cite":{"key":"jacobs-1999","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":", Lemma 1.9.7)."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Strong":[{"Text":"For families."}]},{"Text":" In "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"families of types"}]}},{"Text":", take "},{"Math":{"src":"X' = ∑_((x, y') : X × Y') (f x = h y')"}},{"Text":" with "},{"Math":{"src":"g"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"f'"}},{"Text":" the projections. For "},{"Math":{"src":"A : X -> bold(\"Type\")"}},{"Text":","}]},{"Math":{"src":"(h^* scripts(∑)_(f) A) thin y' = ∑_(x : X) (f x = h y') × A thin x"}},{"Math":{"src":"(scripts(∑)_(f^prime) g^* A) thin y' = ∑_((x, y'', p) : X') (y'' = y') ×\nA thin x"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"and the second contracts to the first, since "},{"Math":{"src":"∑_(y'' : Y') (y'' = y')"}},{"Text":" is contractible. The same contraction under a "},{"Math":{"src":"∏"}},{"Text":" gives "},{"Math":{"src":"(h^*\nscripts(∏)_(f) A) thin y' ≅ (scripts(∏)_(f^prime) g^* A) thin y'"}},{"Text":"."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Along a product projection "},{"Math":{"src":"pi_1 : Y × Z -> Y"}},{"Text":" the adjoints "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∑)_(pi_1)"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"scripts(∏)_(pi_1)"}},{"Text":" are the "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"existential"}]}},{"Text":" and "},{"Span":{"role":"","attrs":[],"body":[{"Text":"universal"}]}},{"Text":" quantifiers, and the squares with sides "},{"Math":{"src":"u × sans(\"id\")"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"u"}},{"Text":" are pullbacks, so Beck–Chevalley for them says that quantification commutes with substitution in the free variables ("},{"Cite":{"key":"jacobs-1999","supplement":null,"rendered":"[1]"}},{"Text":", after Definition 1.9.4)."}]}]}}}]}}
